# Lotto — commit to dev vs ship

Project root: `/opt/apps/lotto-predictore`

## What runs where

| Piece | Role |
| ----- | ---- |
| Git branch `dev` | Integration history on GitHub (CI runs here) |
| Git branch `main` | Not used for lotto releases — do not merge dev → main for deploy |
| Live tree `/opt/apps/lotto-predictore` | Server checkout; `docker compose` bind-mounts `./backend`, `./cron`, `./email-service` |
| Workflow **CI** | Pytest + email smoke on push to `dev` |
| Workflow **Deploy** | Manual dispatch only (`/ship`); checks out frozen SHA on the server |

Saving code on the server is visible to containers immediately via bind mounts, but **GitHub `dev` and recorded releases** only move when you commit/push or ship.

## Which command to use

| Situation | Command | Runs Deploy? | Updates `origin/dev`? |
| --------- | ------- | ------------ | --------------------- |
| Day-to-day work; keep tests green on GitHub | `/commit-dev-until-green` | **no** | **yes** (push `HEAD:dev`) |
| Promote a **frozen, CI-green** `origin/dev` commit to the live stack | `/ship` | **yes** | no (reads remote tip) |

**Non-negotiable:** `/commit-dev-until-green` never dispatches Deploy and never merges to `main`. `/ship` never commits WIP — dirty tracked files block release; integrate first.

## Ship gates (machine)

1. `origin/dev` tip is `FROZEN_SHA` (no unpushed local-only commits).
2. `scripts/gha/verify-ci-green-for-sha.sh "$FROZEN_SHA"` passes.
3. Deploy workflow `confirm` must equal `DEPLOY <sha> TO PRODUCTION` (built by the agent, not a second human prompt).

Extension details: `.cursor/extensions/commit-dev-until-green.md`, `.cursor/extensions/ship.md`.
